# help lists every command.
program: shell
keys: help\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>help
  help     these lines
  echo     echo TEXT: write TEXT
  clear    clear the screen
  dir      dir [PATH]: a directory's files, or a file's line
  cd       cd [PATH]: show or change a drive's directory
  type     type FILE: show a file
  print    print FILE: send a file to the printer on LPT1
  beep     a short tone on the speaker
  play     a tune on the speaker
  joy      the game port's buttons and axes
  mouse    follow the mouse on COM1, until Esc
  term     a terminal on COM2 (a modem), until Esc
  uptime   time since the kernel started
  date     the date and time of the real-time clock
  keys     show each key's scancode and ASCII, until Esc
  fpu      the square root of 2 and pi, by the 80287
  mem      the shell's own segments, as the CPU sees them
  crash    crash KIND: try what no program may (crash help)
  spin     loop forever; Ctrl+Break gets the shell back
  exit     end the shell; the kernel starts it again
  A: B: C: D: make that drive the current one
Keys: Backspace, Esc (clear the line), Up (the last line);
Ctrl+Break restarts the shell, Ctrl+Alt+Del the machine.
A:\>
